AMBER14SB protein + OL24 DNA + ff99bsc0-chiOL3 RNA

********************************************************************
* This force field is assembled at installation time. It is NOT a  *
* redistributed copy of any upstream package.                      *
*                                                                  *
* Protein, water, ions, phosphorylated residues:                   *
*   the GROMACS 2026 ff14SB port bundled with GMXBUILDER, byte for *
*   byte. Converted and validated by Vedran Miletic, Milosz        *
*   Wieczor, Markus Rampp, Carsten Kutzner, Bert L. de Groot and   *
*   Vytautas Gapsys.                                               *
*                                                                  *
* DNA and RNA:                                                     *
*   the nucleic-acid half of amber14sb_OL24.ff, downloaded from    *
*   https://fch.upol.cz/ff_ol/ and verified against a pinned       *
*   SHA-256. Residue databases are taken verbatim; parameters are  *
*   added only where the nucleic acids need them and no residue    *
*   already supported can reach them.                              *
*                                                                  *
* The base carries the plain ff99 glycosidic torsion for           *
* OS-CT-N*-CK and OS-CT-N*-CM. Those are replaced with the refined *
* chiOL profile -- that replacement is what the OL series is for.  *
* All four atom types are nucleic-only, so no protein is affected. *
*                                                                  *
* Cite, for the protein:                                           *
*   Maier, J. A. et al. ff14SB. J. Chem. Theory Comput. 11,        *
*   3696-3713 (2015). doi:10.1021/acs.jctc.5b00255                 *
*   Miletic, V. et al. ChemRxiv (2026).                            *
*                                                                  *
* Cite, for DNA (OL24 and the refinements it builds on):           *
*   Zgarbova, M. et al. J. Chem. Theory Comput. 21, 833-846 (2025) *
*   Zgarbova, M. et al. J. Chem. Theory Comput. 17, 6292 (2021)    *
*   Zgarbova, M. et al. J. Chem. Theory Comput. 11, 5723 (2015)    *
*   Zgarbova, M. et al. J. Chem. Theory Comput. 9, 2339 (2013)     *
*   Perez, A. et al. Biophys. J. 92, 3817 (2007)                   *
*                                                                  *
* Cite, for RNA (ff99bsc0 + chiOL3):                               *
*   Zgarbova, M. et al. J. Chem. Theory Comput. 7, 2886 (2011)     *
*   Perez, A. et al. Biophys. J. 92, 3817 (2007)                   *
*                                                                  *
* Verified against the unmodified upstream port on a hexanucleotide*
* single point: bond, angle, proper-dihedral and Coulomb(SR)       *
* energies are identical. Impropers differ by 0.004 kJ/mol because *
* this force field enables _FF_AMBER_LEAP_ATOM_REORDERING, which   *
* the 2019-era upstream port predates; removing that define        *
* reproduces the upstream value exactly. 1-4 terms differ by 1e-5  *
* relative because the bundled files carry more significant        *
* figures (fudgeQQ 0.83333333333333333 against 0.8333).            *
********************************************************************
